(IN THE GENERAL DIVISION OF THE HIGH COURT) Tj
T*
(OF THE REPUBLIC OF SINGAPORE) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
(Suit No 208 of 2026) Tj
T*
T*
(Between) Tj
T*
(    MERIDIAN COLD CHAIN PTE LTD                        ... Plaintiff) Tj
T*
(And) Tj
T*
(    SEALANE PROVISIONS PTE LTD                         ... Defendant) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 10.5 Tf
(RECORD OF EXAMINATION OF THE DEFENDANT'S PROCUREMENT MANAGER) Tj
T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
(Taken on 21 May 2026 at 10.00 am) Tj
T*
T*
(Present:  Ms Serene Koh \(Counsel for the Plaintiff\)) Tj
T*
(          Mr Arun Pillai \(Counsel for the Defendant\)) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(Q1.  Please state your name and position.) Tj
T*
(A.   Goh Mei Ling. I am the procurement manager at Sealane Provisions.) Tj
T*
(     I have held that role since 2021.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q2.  Were you responsible for the supply agreement with Meridian?) Tj
T*
(A.   Yes. I negotiated it and I signed it on behalf of Sealane on) Tj
T*
(     4 February 2025.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q3.  Clause 7 provides for delivery of chilled stock within a two hour) Tj
T*
(     window. Was that clause discussed before signing?) Tj
T*
(A.   It was in their standard terms. We asked for three hours. Their) Tj
T*
(     sales director said the two hour window was fixed but that they) Tj
T*
(     would be reasonable in practice.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q4.  Was that assurance recorded anywhere?) Tj
T*
(A.   Not in the contract. It was in an email dated 22 January 2025 and) Tj
T*
(     again at a meeting at their Tuas facility.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q5.  Clause 12 is a liquidated damages clause of $4,000 per late) Tj
T*
(     delivery. How was that figure arrived at?) Tj
T*
(A.   I don't recall any calculation being shown to us. It was in the) Tj
T*
(     draft when we received it.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q6.  Did Sealane ever ask how the figure was estimated?) Tj
T*
(A.   I asked once. I was told it reflected their exposure to the) Tj
T*
(     supermarkets downstream. No breakdown was provided.) Tj
T*
ET
