/F1 10.5 Tf
(Q7.  Between March and August 2025, how many deliveries were late?) Tj
T*
(A.   By our log book, fourteen. Meridian's records say nine. The) Tj
T*
(     difference is deliveries where the driver arrived within the) Tj
T*
(     window but the cold room was not opened until later.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q8.  Who operated the cold room?) Tj
T*
(A.   A third party. Our warehousing is outsourced to Northgate) Tj
T*
(     Logistics. They are an independent contractor engaged under a) Tj
T*
(     separate agreement.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q9.  Did Sealane instruct Northgate on receiving procedures?) Tj
T*
(A.   We gave them the delivery schedule. How they staff the dock is) Tj
T*
(     their operation. We do not supervise their workers.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q10. On 3 September 2025 Sealane purported to terminate the agreement.) Tj
T*
(     On what basis?) Tj
T*
(A.   Repeated late deliveries. Our position was that the breaches were) Tj
T*
(     serious enough to go to the root of the contract.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q11. Did Sealane give notice before terminating?) Tj
T*
(A.   We sent two warning letters, in June and in July.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q12. Was any product actually spoiled?) Tj
T*
(A.   On four occasions. We disposed of the stock and claimed against) Tj
T*
(     Meridian. There is a spoilage report for each occasion.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q13. Were photographs taken of the spoiled stock?) Tj
T*
(A.   I believe so. I have not personally seen all of them.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q14. After termination, did Sealane source from an alternative supplier?) Tj
T*
(A.   Yes, from 15 September, at a higher unit price. That difference is) Tj
T*
(     part of our counterclaim.) Tj
T*
T*
(Q15. Is there anything you wish to correct in your earlier evidence?) Tj
T*
(A.   Only that the meeting at Tuas was in January, not February. I am) Tj
T*
(     not sure of the exact date.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
